{
 "source": "trapp",
 "book": "MRK",
 "chapter": 15,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.1",
   "range": "MRK.15.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a1589659",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.1#p1-a1589659",
     "text": "They thought once to have deferred his execution till after the feast, Mar 14:2. But their malice was restless, as his was that said he would not away till he saw the martyr’s (the traitor’s he called him) heart out.",
     "anchor": "And straightway in the morning",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:2",
       "ref": "MRK.14.2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.2",
   "range": "MRK.15.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ad8982f3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.2#p1-ad8982f3",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 27:1\"} {See Trapp on \"Mat 27:2\"} {See Trapp on \"Mat 27:3\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:1",
       "ref": "MAT.27.1"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:2",
       "ref": "MAT.27.2"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:3",
       "ref": "MAT.27.3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.3",
   "range": "MRK.15.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0d89108e",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.3#p1-0d89108e",
     "text": "Or, at each great feast, καθ εορτην, viz. at the Passover, Pentecost, and Tabernacles. The reason of this custom: {See Trapp on \"Mat 27:15\"}",
     "anchor": "Now at the feast",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:15",
       "ref": "MAT.27.15"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.7",
   "range": "MRK.15.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "817dd491",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.7#p1-817dd491",
     "text": "Purposely to move the people to pity him, and therefore brought him forth so misused, with, \"Behold the man.\" But this was ill done of Pilate nevertheless, as was also his comparing with Barabbas, though with intent so to have delivered him. For we may not do evil that good may come thereof.",
     "anchor": "When he had scourged him"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.21",
   "range": "MRK.15.21",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "76fe85fd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.21#p1-be62c35c",
     "text": "αγγαρευουσι, cogunt invitum. We all come off heavily, and shrink in the shoulder when called to carry the cross, as Peter did, Joh 21:18.",
     "anchor": "And they compel one Simon",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 21:18",
       "ref": "JHN.21.18"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.21#p2-b45df84d",
     "text": "Men famously known in the Church, and therefore here but named only. God will recompense even involuntary services.",
     "anchor": "The father of Alexander and Rufus"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.22",
   "range": "MRK.15.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d01cdd34",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.22#p1-d01cdd34",
     "text": "St Mark very diligently describeth what happened at Calvary; what Christ did and said on the cross, what was done and said to him there, how he gave up the ghost, &c., that we might have these things as ready, and at our fingers’ ends, as he had who wrote the whole history of our Saviour’s passion upon the nails of his hands."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.23",
   "range": "MRK.15.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "807b1866",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.23#p1-807b1866",
     "text": "This was not the same potion with that in Mar 15:36; Mat 27:48, but another.",
     "anchor": "Wine mingled with myrrh",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 15:36",
       "ref": "MRK.15.36"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:48",
       "ref": "MAT.27.48"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.24",
   "range": "MRK.15.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "5973d411",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.24#p1-5973d411",
     "text": "i.e. they began to crucify him, but nailed him not to the tree till the sixth hour, Joh 19:14.",
     "anchor": "They crucified him",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 19:14",
       "ref": "JHN.19.14"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.26",
   "range": "MRK.15.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "32c7b8f6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.26#p1-32c7b8f6",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 27:37\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:37",
       "ref": "MAT.27.37"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.27",
   "range": "MRK.15.27",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ecbd3b92",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.27#p1-ecbd3b92",
     "text": "Portending doubtless those dreadful calamities that were coming upon this perverse people, according to Isa 5:30; Isa 8:22; Lam 3:1-2; but clearly showing God’s heavy displeasure against his Son, our surety, which made him also cry out with a loud voice in the next verse, as one so far forsaken, as not afforded the common benefit of sunlight.",
     "anchor": "Darkness over the whole land",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Isa 5:30",
       "ref": "ISA.5.30"
      },
      {
       "text": "Isa 8:22",
       "ref": "ISA.8.22"
      },
      {
       "text": "Lam 3:1-2",
       "ref": "LAM.3.1-2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.34",
   "range": "MRK.15.34",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "52ba0cf9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.34#p1-52ba0cf9",
     "text": "Psa 22:1. It is thought by some that he repeated the whole of Psa 22:1-31, which is an admirable narration of the passion, and might well help him the better to bear it.",
     "anchor": "Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Psa 22:1",
       "ref": "PSA.22.1"
      },
      {
       "text": "Psa 22:1-31",
       "ref": "PSA.22.1-31"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.35",
   "range": "MRK.15.35",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0013b8bb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.35#p1-0013b8bb",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 27:47\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:47",
       "ref": "MAT.27.47"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.36",
   "range": "MRK.15.36",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "08bde5bb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.36#p1-08bde5bb",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 27:48\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 27:48",
       "ref": "MAT.27.48"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.37",
   "range": "MRK.15.37",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "206ec4bb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.15.37#p1-206ec4bb",
     "text": "After which he went not to Limbus Patrum to preach there, as Papists dote, and would deduce it from 1Pe 3:19.",
     "anchor": "He gave up the ghost",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Pe 3:19",
       "ref": "1PE.3.19"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.15.38",
   "range": "MRK.15.38",
   "kind": "passage",
